==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Pharaoh Reika''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Eternal Reika''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Reika can be used to defeat [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] and [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] enemies with ease since she does massive damage against them and has Zombie Killer. She can OHKO many Zombie units and even get rid of those that revive an unlimited number of times (like [[Zamelle]]). Her quick attack animation even allows her to hit Zombies before they burrow, though this can be quite difficult to pull off. She even is able to succeed against [[Li'l Zyclone|Li'l Zyclone]] and [[Dread Bore]], two of the most dangerous Zombie enemies in the game. Against [[Cadaver Bear]], she works well, but due to Cadaver's attack rate, it is highly recommended you use highly levelled meatshields or tankers like [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell Cat]] and [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] to stall him, else she will not be able to consistently hit him.

Reika can be used in tandem with other [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Aliens]]/[[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|anti-Zombies]] to make even easier work of them. However, you should focus on using Cats that support her instead of secondary attackers, as Reika is already prone to miss. Cats that debuff (ex. [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-controllers]] like [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]]) are the most ideal for this role.

Her multi-hit can partially damage incoming enemies via the second hit. However, enemies can also "dodge" the second hit if they are knocked back. An advantage of this is that it can work for crowd-control, so freezing the Alien before she starts to land the second hit is a guaranteed way of letting her do damage.

==='''True Form'''===
Reika gains 2 additional knockbacks and an increased attack rate. The additional knockbacks improve her survivability by a whole lot against powerful pushing enemies such as [[Dread Bore]]/[[Nimoy Bore]], therefore letting Reika stay alive longer. In addition, her attack rate is shortened by 2.8 seconds, letting her land more hits along with the boosted DPS.

==='''Talents'''===
Her '''Target Relic''' and [[Immune to Curse]] Talents open up so many doors involving Relic enemies, she effectively becomes a second [[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]]. Although Luza does have more on-hit damage and more range, Reika has the benefit of higher and consistent DPS, other targets in general, and higher base range than Luza. Considering you can unlock these Talents as soon as you enter Uncanny Legends, it's safe to say Reika will likely be useful for a long time.

At max level, '''[[Special Abilities#Resist|Resist Slow]]''' functions nearly identically to full immunity and works great against the likes of [[Lophiiformes Angaburu]] and surprise [[Zomboe]]s. However, due to its heightened cost, and the infrequency of occasions where it would be majorly helpful, it isn't recommended to invest in this Talent if you aren't already using Reika on a regular basis. HP and Attack Buff are nice to have obviously, but boosting her first using [[Catseye]]s is recommended.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
'''[[Sage Slayer]]''' has four main targets, those being [[Oldstrich]], [[Techn-Old Hyena]], [[Sage of Selection Darvin]], and [[Shachiko]]. Oldstrich is somewhat tanky, and because of this, Reika can usually get both hits off on them, basically vaporizing a fourth of their HP on the spot. This makes them her best matchup by far. Reika completely outranges Techn-Old Hyena's Omni Strike, but her DPH is usually so high that she staggers them after the first hit, so her full-potential is sometimes halved. Sage of Selection Darvin gets countered pretty hard by Ultra Talented Reika, completely nuking [[Commander Ostromeda]] out of existence and bringing that fire to Darvin right afterwards. These Ultra Talents may be worth unlocking if you find yourself struggling on [[Endless Forms Most Beautiful]]. Shachiko is not a particularly practical use-case, since it doesn't normally find itself in the crossfire of Reika's attack in the heat of battle. Oftentimes, it's less of a headache to simply nuke it out of existence with [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:NX]] than deal with it normally. As a general Sage Slayer, she's alright, outranging most common Sages and being Resistant to their status effects makes her a fairly safe pick all-around. Her DPS isn't the highest against non-targets, however.

'''Attack Frequency Up''' increases her DPS by a whopping ~20.7%, being effectively a second Attack Buff that specifically pairs well with her final Ultra Talent. If any Ultra Talent is worth considering in this bunch, it's this one.

'''[[Slow]]''' is absurd. Assuming an enemy is struck by both of her Multi-Hits, the ability has an average uptime of ~49.8% against Aliens/Zombies, and ~43.9% against Relics. This Role Compression can eliminate the need for a dedicated crowd-controller against many high-pressure threats like Commander Ostromeda, Oldstrich, [[M. Ost]], [[Relic Bun-Bun]], [[Dread Bore|Dread]]/[[Nimoy Bore]], and the list goes on. Moreover, maxing out Reika's Attack Frequency Up Talent brings the uptime up to 60% against Aliens/Zombies, and ~52.9% against Relics, and owning Sage Slayer allows you reliably apply this debuff on Sages. On its own, this Ultra Talent is fantastic, but it burgeons into a powerhouse investment with everything else unlocked.

Fittingly for a queen, bringing her to optimal performance is extremely costly: excluding Resist Slow and Defense Buff, these Talents cost a massive 1,035 NP. Consider whether her dominant matchups are relevant to your current place in the game, as most of them only appear in [[Zero Legends]]. If they do, however, her destructive power is essentially unmatched. 

==='''Orbs'''===
Two Massive Damage orbs against Aliens, Zombies, or Relics. For ability orbs, Strengthen is the way to go.

